message: "If you use PeterPiper in your research, please cite it as below and name the version you used."
title: "PeterPiper: single-cell fluorescence time-course analysis for Nikon .nd2 movies"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/peterdepaola4/PeterPiper"
url: "https://github.com/peterdepaola4/PeterPiper"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24120837"
authors:
  - family-names: DePaola
    given-names: Peter
    name-suffix: IV
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4264-0375"
    affiliation: "Schmitt Lab, University of California, Los Angeles"
keywords:
  - fluorescence microscopy
  - live-cell imaging
  - single-cell analysis
  - cell tracking
  - ratiometric imaging
  - Nikon ND2
  - GraphPad Prism
abstract: >-
  PeterPiper (formerly PD4nav; version 1.0 continues PD4nav 3.0) measures fluorescence in single cells over time in Nikon NIS-Elements
  .nd2 time-lapse movies. Regions of interest (nucleus, cytoplasm, whole cell,
  mitochondria) are drawn from the image, followed through every timepoint by
  redrawing them from that timepoint's pixels, measured in every channel with a
  per-timepoint background, and exported to Excel, GraphPad Prism (with the
  graphs made), CSV and images, together with a methods text and full
  provenance. Saved runs can be compared and averaged as replicate dishes
  (mean of dish means, n = dishes), one measure can be plotted against another,
  and response kinetics (t1/2, initial slope) are computed per dish.
